.el .ds Aq '
.TH FATHOM_SEARCH 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-search \- Search the whole index from one box, in the shell\*(Aqs own ranking (`e5.2`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom search\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-save\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIQUERY\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Search the whole index from one box, in the shell\*(Aqs own ranking (`e5.2`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to read
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the report as one JSON line on stdout (`fathom.search/1`)
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR [default: 20]
How many hits to print
.TP
\fB\-\-save\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Keep this query under a name, so the `,` palette can offer it again
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
List the saved searches and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIQUERY\fR]
The query, with the same filter tokens `/` takes (`author:`, `since:`, `risk>`, `path:`, `dep:`, …)
